{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>who was born to Bethuel son of Milcah.</b> Because Nahor had sons from his concubine Reumah, Scripture always traces his lineage as \"Bethuel son of Milcah.\" And because the girl mentioned her father's mother first — \"I am the daughter of Bethuel son of Milcah\" — for so is the way of maidens, as in \"and she told her mother's house\" (Genesis 24:28) — therefore Scripture mentions that he is the son of Milcah, the wife of Nahor. But the servant said, \"and she said, the daughter of Bethuel son of Nahor\" (v. 47), for he set the matter in proper form, yet he said \"whom Milcah bore to him,\" to say that he is the son of the mistress."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:33:56.863520710Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}